{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8DxNYoraF65aVZuKS5r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The description covers only `apply`: it rejects zero-quantity `Restock`/`Sell` changes with `ZeroQuantity` and repeat `Discontinue` changes with `AlreadyDiscontinued`. The changes to `ApplyError` (lines 36–39) and to `apply` (lines 70–72 and 85–87) do exactly that. They use no capabilities and send nothing to the output sinks.\n\nThe diff also adds things the description doesn't mention:\n\n- The import is widened to bring in `std::fs::Fs` and `io` (line 1).\n- `LoadError` gains a new `Io(io::Error)` variant (line 28).\n- There is a new public function `load_file(fs: &Fs, path: &str)` (lines 52–53). It takes a file-system capability and reads any path the caller names.\n\nBefore this change, the library had no I/O at all. `load` and `apply` take bytes and `save` returns bytes. `load_file` is a new public function that holds the `Fs` capability and uses it to read files. Nothing about rejecting no-op changes calls for this, so the change takes authority its description does not call for.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"reject\", \"findings\": [{\"line\": 52, \"item\": \"load_file\", \"authority\": \"fs\", \"what\": \"Adds a new public function that holds an `Fs` capability and reads an arbitrary caller-supplied file path, which rejecting no-op changes in `apply` does not call for.\"}]}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":5837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d7900f-34a0-49af-a3ff-39eaba168877","uuid":"65bb01a9-f9dd-423d-a725-aeb041